---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      "headline": "The Ultimate Zhangjiajie National Park Guide (2026)",
      "description": "Everything you need to know before visiting Zhangjiajie: tickets, transportation, hiking routes, where to stay, and insider tips for 2026.",
      "datePublished": "2026-07-01",
      "dateModified": "2026-07-31",
      "author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Zhangjiajie Guide Team"}
    },
    { "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://zhangjiajie-national-park.com/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Complete Guide", "item": "https://zhangjiajie-national-park.com/guide/" }
    ]}
  ]
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="The Ultimate Zhangjiajie National Park Guide (2026)"
  description="Everything you need to know before visiting Zhangjiajie National Park: tickets, transport options, best hiking routes, where to stay in Wulingyuan, insider tips, and prices verified April 2026."
  author="Zhangjiajie Guide Team"
  datePublished="July 2026"
>
  <slot name="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)}></script>
  </slot>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 md:px-6 pb-20 md:pb-28">
    <div class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-forest-200 bg-forest-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-forest-700 mb-6">Complete Guide</div>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-900 leading-tight">The Ultimate Zhangjiajie National Park Guide</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">
      Zhangjiajie National Forest Park is China's first national park and a <a href="https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/640" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-forest-600 hover:text-forest-700 underline">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>. This guide covers everything we have learned from multiple visits: tickets, transport, hiking routes, where to stay, what to pack, and how to avoid the crowds.
    </p>
    <nav class="mt-6 flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-stone-400" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-forest-700 transition-colors">Home</a>
      <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M6 3l5 5-5 5"/></svg>
      <span class="text-stone-600">Complete Guide</span>
    </nav>
    

  <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden">
    <picture>
      <source srcset="/banner-guide.webp" type="image/webp" />
      <img
        src="/banner-guide.jpg"
        alt="Panoramic sandstone pillars of Zhangjiajie National Forest Park"
        class="w-full aspect-[21/9] object-cover"
        width="1200"
        height="514"
        loading="eager"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </picture>
  </div>
    <div class="mt-12 space-y-16">
      <!-- Getting There -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">How to Get There</h2>
        <p class="text-stone-500 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Zhangjiajie has its own airport (DYG) with direct flights from Beijing, Shanghai, Guangzhou, and Chengdu. The high-speed train station (Zhangjiajie West) connects to Changsha in under 3 hours — we have taken this route three times and consistently arrive in 2 hours 45 minutes. From downtown, the park's Wulingyuan entrance is a 40-minute bus or taxi ride.
        </p>
        <p class="text-stone-500 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          On our latest trip in April 2026, a taxi from Zhangjiajie West station to Wulingyuan town cost CNY 95 including the meter. The bus is CNY 12 and leaves every 10 minutes from the central bus station — look for the blue minibuses marked "Wulingyuan" in Chinese characters (武陵源).
        </p>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-stone-50 p-5 text-sm text-stone-600">
          <strong class="text-stone-800">Pro tip:</strong> Fly into Changsha and take the high-speed train to Zhangjiajie. Changsha has far more international connections, and the combined flight + train is often cheaper than a direct Zhangjiajie flight. We saved CNY 800 per person doing this in April 2026.
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Park Zones -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">Park Zones Explained</h2>
        <p class="text-stone-500 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          "Zhangjiajie" actually refers to four separate scenic areas, each with its own entrance and ticket. Here is what we found each one offers — and what is worth skipping if your time is tight:
        </p>
        <div class="grid gap-4">
          {[
            { name: "Zhangjiajie National Forest Park", highlight: "The core. Avatar mountains, Golden Whip Stream, Yuanjiajie. This is what most people picture when they think of Zhangjiajie.", time: "1-2 days", verdict: "Non-negotiable", href: "/attractions" },
            { name: "Tianmen Mountain", highlight: "Heaven's Gate arch, 999-step staircase, cliff-hanging walkway. The cable car ride alone (7.5 km from downtown) is worth the entry fee.", time: "Half day", verdict: "Do not miss", href: "/tianmen-mountain" },
            { name: "Zhangjiajie Grand Canyon", highlight: "World's longest and highest glass-bottom bridge. The bridge is the draw; the canyon hike below is optional but pleasant.", time: "Half day", verdict: "If you have 3+ days", href: "/glass-bridge" },
            { name: "Tianzi Mountain Nature Reserve", highlight: "Sea of clouds at sunrise, panoramic pillar views. Connects directly to Yuanjiajie by shuttle bus, so you will pass through anyway.", time: "Half day", verdict: "Part of the core circuit", href: "/attractions" },
          ].map(({ name, highlight, time, verdict, href }) => (
            <a href={href} class="block no-underline rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-5 transition-all hover:border-forest-200 hover:shadow-md">
              <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4">
                <div>
                  <h3 class="font-semibold text-stone-800 group-hover:text-forest-700">{name}</h3>
                  <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">{highlight}</p>
                </div>
                <div class="shrink-0 text-right">
                  <span class="inline-block rounded-full bg-forest-50 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-forest-700 whitespace-nowrap">{time}</span>
                  <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-stone-400">{verdict}</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Tickets -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">Tickets & Costs</h2>
        <p class="text-stone-500 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          The main park ticket is valid for 4 consecutive days and covers entry plus internal shuttle buses. Cable cars, the Bailong Elevator, and in-park transport cost extra. Budget around CNY 500—800 per person for a full visit including transport inside the park. All prices verified at the Wulingyuan gate, April 2026.
        </p>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-5 mb-4">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-3">
            <span class="font-semibold text-stone-800">Park Entry (4-day pass)</span>
            <span class="text-sm text-stone-400">Peak / Off-peak</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <span class="text-2xl font-semibold text-forest-700">&yen;225</span>
            <span class="text-stone-500">&yen;115</span>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-stone-400">Student & senior discounts available. Children under 1.2m and seniors 70+ enter free.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/tickets" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-forest-500 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white transition-all hover:bg-forest-600 active:scale-[0.98]">
          Full Ticket Breakdown & Buying Guide
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 3l5 5-5 5"/></svg>
        </a>
      </section>

      <!-- Where to Stay -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">Where to Stay</h2>
        <p class="text-stone-500 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Wulingyuan town (near the park entrance) is the most convenient base — we have stayed here on four separate trips and never regretted it. The town has everything: restaurants, convenience stores, ATMs, and hotels ranging from CNY 150 guesthouses to the CNY 800 Pullman.
        </p>
        <p class="text-stone-500 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Zhangjiajie city center is about CNY 100/night cheaper on average, but you add 40 minutes of travel each way. That is nearly 90 minutes of commuting per day — time better spent inside the park. A handful of guesthouses operate inside the park itself (near Huangshi Village) for photographers who want sunrise access. We stayed at one in November 2025. Basic but magical.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Insider Tips -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">Insider Tips</h2>
        <p class="text-stone-500 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">Things we learned the hard way, so you do not have to.</p>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-stone-500 text-sm">
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-forest-600 shrink-0 mt-0.5">&bull;</span> <strong class="text-stone-700">Enter before 8 AM.</strong> Tour groups arrive at 9. The first hour inside the park — mist still hanging in the valleys, zero crowds — is the best hour of the day. We have never regretted an early start.</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-forest-600 shrink-0 mt-0.5">&bull;</span> <strong class="text-stone-700">Bring cash.</strong> Many snack stalls and smaller vendors do not accept foreign cards or international WeChat Pay. CNY 500 in small bills will cover a full day of water, snacks, and souvenirs.</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-forest-600 shrink-0 mt-0.5">&bull;</span> <strong class="text-stone-700">Pack a rain jacket even on sunny days.</strong> The weather in the mountains shifts fast. The mist is half the magic, but being soaked is not.</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-forest-600 shrink-0 mt-0.5">&bull;</span> <strong class="text-stone-700">Stay inside the park for sunrise.</strong> The guesthouses near Huangshi Village let you photograph the pillars with zero crowds. We did this in November and had Tianzi Mountain entirely to ourselves at 7 AM.</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-forest-600 shrink-0 mt-0.5">&bull;</span> <strong class="text-stone-700">Download offline maps.</strong> Cell signal inside the park is patchy, especially in the valleys. Download the area in Google Maps or Maps.me before you go.</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-forest-600 shrink-0 mt-0.5">&bull;</span> <strong class="text-stone-700">Passport everywhere.</strong> Foreign visitors must show their passport at every ticket checkpoint. No photocopies accepted. Keep it in a waterproof pouch.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-16 pt-12 border-t border-stone-200 text-center">
      <p class="text-stone-500 mb-6">Ready to pick your dates?</p>
      <a href="/best-time-to-visit" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-forest-500 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white transition-all hover:bg-forest-600 active:scale-[0.98]">
        Best Time to Visit
        <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 3l5 5-5 5" /></svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
